      "id": 1,
      "text": "Glen Haven was originally named Stump Town before being renamed Ray's Landing for roughly two decades.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitglenhavenwi.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "With the arrival of the railroad in 1884, Glen Haven became a major shipping point for livestock between St. Paul and Chicago.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitglenhavenwi.com/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Known as the Village in the Valley, Glen Haven is tucked between the Mississippi River and a ring of protective hills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://wigrr.com/community/glen-haven/"
    },
    {
